"""Foreground alignment of a still-visual motion with its reference image, as a number (16 October 2026).

For each visual a few colour masks pick the foreground ink (the pink word, the white title, the dark text on orange...) inside a region where the picture does not interfere; the same masks are computed
on the reference still and on the motion frame (HyperFrames snapshot), and compared: IoU (exact overlap) and DIoU (overlap after a 3 px tolerance, which forgives anti-aliasing but not a shifted or resized word).
An overlay image shows the reference ink in red, the motion ink in cyan and the overlap in white: what is red alone is missing, what is cyan alone is in the wrong place.
FR : un nombre d'alignement du premier plan (recouvrement des encres), plus une image qui montre l'ecart.
Usage: python3 Scripts/MaskIoU.py <project-id> [--at 4] [--out DIR]   (reference = the still named by the project)
"""
